message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good evening, Mr. ___ . I'm Dr. ___ , one of your hospital doctors. You were admitted for a fever and some concerns about your kidney function. How are you feeling right now?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Evening, Doctor. I’m okay, no fever now. But I was worried—my blood pressure’s been really high at home, like over 200. That scared me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your blood pressure was 208 over 98 when you arrived. That’s definitely too high. We’re restarting your usual medications—labetalol, nifedipine, and minoxidil—and we’ve increased your clonidine patch to 0.2 mg to help control it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I forgot to take a couple of my pills before coming in. But is the fever from an infection? My leg wound’s been okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We checked for infections—blood cultures, urine, flu test—all negative. No signs of wound infection either. The fever might have been a mild viral thing. You haven’t had a fever since arriving, which is reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good to hear. But my kidney numbers were high—creatinine 4.0. Is that from dehydration?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. You mentioned poor appetite lately. We gave you IV fluids, but your kidney function didn’t improve much. That’s why we’re planning a kidney biopsy tomorrow to check for other causes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Biopsy? Is that safe? I’m on blood thinners."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s very safe. We’ll use ultrasound to guide the needle, and your INR is normal. We’ll hold your spironolactone and chlorthalidone—they can affect kidneys—and monitor closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. And my pain meds—can I keep taking the OxyContin 30 mg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re reducing it to 20 mg twice daily. Your kidneys aren’t filtering as well, so we need to lower the dose to avoid side effects. You’ll still get breakthrough pain meds if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I understand. And gabapentin—I take 300 mg three times a day."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re cutting that to 100 mg once daily for the same reason. We’ll keep the nortriptyline and Tylenol. We want to manage pain safely without overloading your system."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. What about my hand and leg wounds? They’re still painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The vascular and plastic surgery teams looked at them. No signs of infection. The leg wound has good granulation tissue, but the Achilles tendon is still exposed. They want to see you after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no more wound vac?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2152-10-09 04:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not for now. We’ll switch to wet-to-dry dressings at home. The vac helped, but now it’s about protecting the area until they decide on next steps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We did the kidney biopsy this morning under ultrasound guidance. It went smoothly—three passes, no complications."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How did it go? Did they find anything?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The tissue looked good—no rejection. But there’s scarring in the filters—glomerulosclerosis—and some artery hardening. Likely from long-term high blood pressure and vascular disease."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So not rejection. That’s a relief. But the kidneys are still getting worse?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but it’s not sudden. Your creatinine dropped from 4.0 to 3.2 after fluids and monitoring. We’ll keep working on blood pressure control to slow further damage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the BK virus? I’m on leflunomide."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your BK virus level is low—under 500—so we’ll keep you on leflunomide. The transplant team will follow up on that and check for donor antibodies, which are pending."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my leg bypass—did they check the stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we did a duplex ultrasound yesterday. The popliteal to dorsalis pedis graft is widely patent—good flow. That’s great news for circulation to your foot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2152-10-10 08:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. I was worried it might be blocked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Morning. Your labs are stable. Creatinine is 3.2, hemoglobin dipped a bit, so we gave one unit of blood yesterday for your chronic anemia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t feel low, but okay. Any fever? Infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No fever at all. Cultures are negative. We’re confident there’s no infection. Your blood pressure is also better—around 158 over 79 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s much better. So what’s next?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning discharge tomorrow. You’ll go home with home nursing for wound care—wet-to-dry dressings daily. And you need to follow up with plastic surgery and vascular surgery."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When should I call them?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Call plastic surgery on the day after discharge to schedule an appointment. The transplant team will also contact you for a follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my meds—what changes are staying?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll keep the new clonidine patch—0.2 mg, changed weekly. OxyContin is 20 mg twice daily. Gabapentin is 100 mg once daily. And we’re holding spironolactone and chlorthalidone for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So don’t restart those water pills?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Correct. The kidney team will tell you if and when to restart them. Same with your sodium thiosulfate—keep getting it three times a week for calciphylaxis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And insulin? My sugars have been high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2152-10-11 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re still on glargine 14 units at bedtime and a sliding scale. Keep monitoring your sugars and adjust as before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re doing well. We’re finalizing your discharge. Your condition is stable—no fever, better blood pressure, and kidney function is steady."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. So I can go home today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, later this morning. Home nursing will help with your wound care. Remember—wet-to-dry dressings every day until you see the plastic surgeon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And I’ll get my meds as listed?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. You’ll get 10 tablets of the 20 mg OxyContin for the new dose. And the rest are as prescribed. Don’t restart the held meds without calling the kidney team."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use your walker for support. Avoid heavy lifting. Keep your feet clean and dry. Watch for redness, swelling, or fever—and call us if any of those happen."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. The team will call you with biopsy results if anything changes. Otherwise, focus on rest, meds, and follow-up appointments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. I’m glad we figured out it wasn’t rejection or infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s excellent news. Your transplant is stable. We just need to protect it with good blood pressure control and follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep checking my BP at home and take my meds as directed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. That’s the best thing you can do. We’ll get your discharge papers ready, and you should be out by noon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2152-10-12 09:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2152-10-09 03:44:00",
